  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "To like: 좋아해요",
     "texto": [
      "**좋아해요** means «to like», and the thing you like takes the object particle: 저는 김치**를** 좋아해요 = I like kimchi.",
      "The opposite: **안 좋아해요** (I don't like it) or, stronger, **싫어해요** (I can't stand it).",
      "Do not confuse it with **좋아요** («it is good», «OK»), which takes 이/가: 날씨**가** 좋아요."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Wanting to do something: -고 싶어요",
     "texto": [
      "You take the verb stem (the dictionary form without 다) and add **-고 싶어요**.",
      "먹다 → **먹고 싶어요** (I want to eat). 가다 → **가고 싶어요** (I want to go). 마시다 → **마시고 싶어요** (I want to drink).",
      "To ask: **뭐 먹고 싶어요?** = What do you want to eat?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Want + verb",
